[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605215100-etzhayyim-maps-sentinel-mlx-murakumo-fleet", :adr/title "ADR-2605215100: Sentinel-1/2 satellite analysis on Murakumo fleet — tiered MLX/ROCm placement without RunPod", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605215100: Sentinel-1/2 satellite analysis on Murakumo fleet — tiered MLX/ROCm placement without RunPod\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-21\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n---\n\n# Context\n\n## The vendor implementation\n\nThe vendor `kotodama` module at `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/maps_sentinel.py` provides two LangServer task types over Sentinel satellite imagery:\n\n| Task type | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `maps.sentinel.stac.search` | STAC POST /search across Element84 (Sentinel-2 L2A) and Copernicus (Sentinel-1 GRD) STAC catalogs; writes scene rows to `vertex_satellite_scene` |\n| `maps.sentinel.runpod.analyze` | GPU analysis via RunPod Serverless `/run` + `/status` poll; writes result rows to `vertex_satellite_analysis` |\n\nThe `_ANALYSIS_MODELS` registry defines three analysis types routed to RunPod:\n\n| Analysis key | Backend model | Platform |\n|---|---|---|\n| `change_detection` | `sentinel2_change_siamese` (Siamese-CNN multi-temporal diff) | Sentinel-2 |\n| `land_use` | `sentinel2_landuse_unet` (U-Net semantic segmentation) | Sentinel-2 |\n| `sar_flood` | `sentinel1_flood_unet` (U-Net binary flood mask) | Sentinel-1 SAR |\n\nThe wire contract — NSID `com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.sentinelAnalyze` with input fields `sceneUri`, `analysisType` (`changeDetection | landUse | sarFlood`), `baselineUri`, `modelVersion` and output fields `analysisUri`, `summary`, `confidence`, `modelVersion`, `runtimeMs` — is defined in `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/maps/sentinelAnalyze.json`.\n\nThe vendor infrastructure uses RunPod Serverless GPU (approximately a 6000 Ada 48GB class endpoint for heavy workloads, L40S-class for lighter ones). **ADR-2605215000 §2.3 marked `maps_sentinel.py` as REIMPLEMENT** because `task_maps_sentinel_runpod_analyze` is structurally RunPod-dependent: it calls `_runpod_invoke_sync()` which POSTs to `api.runpod.ai`, polls `/status`, and requires `RUNPOD_KEY` and `RUNPOD_ENDPOINT_ID_MAPS`. An env-URL swap is not sufficient — the entire polling pattern and model registry must be replaced.\n\n## Why religious-corp needs this\n\nThe Sentinel analysis capability has direct religious-corp use cases that do not exist in the vendor SaaS product:\n\n1. **Land trust monitoring (ADR-2605192245)** — etzhayyim holds donated land in a 4-layer substrate (Base L2 NFT + geth-private constitutional + IPFS GeoJSON + git LANDS.md). Sentinel-2 vegetation change detection and land-cover classification provide periodic automated stewardship evidence without deploying human witnesses to every parcel.\n\n2. **kuni-umi survey (ADR-2605201400)** — the `SiteSurveyCell` and `AuditWitnessCell` cells use SAR-derived flood maps and change-detection outputs as non-fungible evidence in the Pregel witness chain. Sentinel-1 SAR is especially relevant for coastal and river plots (ADR-2605192330 extended sovereignty).\n\n3. **Community governance** — LandStewardshipMonitoringCell (simeon node, monthly cron) currently has no satellite analysis backend. Once `maps_sentinel_murakumo.py` is operational, the monthly stewardship cycle can include automated scene analysis without RunPod billing.\n\n## Hardware budget\n\nThe religious-corp fleet has two GPU-capable execution environments, both materially inferior to RunPod's 48GB A6000 Ada baseline:\n\n### EVO-X2 (primary GPU node)\n\n- AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395, Radeon 8060S iGPU (RDNA 3.5, gfx1151), 32GB VRAM (BIOS UMA from 128GB unified), 96GB system RAM\n- Windows 11 Pro 24H2, LAN-only `192.168.1.70`, no DID, no AT membership\n- ROCm gfx1151 backend (verified via PyTorch 2.9.1+rocm7.2.1 under ComfyUI portable)\n- **Strengths**: largest single VRAM budget on the fleet; supports vision-language models up to ~16GB; ComfyUI already operational\n- **Weaknesses**: ROCm gfx1151 coverage is narrower than NVIDIA CUDA (not all ONNX backends compile, half-precision support is partial); Windows makes MLX-native inference impossible; no Ollama gemma3:4b fallback for vision tasks; single machine = single point of failure\n- Verified throughput (vision-language class benchmarks not yet run; general LLM: llama3.2:3b at 83 tok/s, llama3.3:70b at 1.18 tok/s)\n\n### Mac mini fleet (10 nodes, Murakumo)\n\n- 10 × Apple Silicon Mac mini (12-tribes naming; naphtali, simeon, judah, zebulun, levi, joseph, issachar, dan, benjamin, asher)\n- Chip generations: M1 (older nodes), M2, M4; unified memory 16–32GB per node\n- **Strengths**: MLX-native (Apple's Metal-accelerated ML framework); 10-node redundancy; launchd-managed; already running 15 Pregel cells; per-node Ollama gemma3:4b fallback\n- **Weaknesses**: per-node VRAM ceiling (max 32GB); no discrete GPU; M1/M2 nodes at 16GB cannot fit anything larger than ~9GB models at 4-bit\n\nPreferred high-memory nodes for satellite inference: **dan** (M4, 32GB), **naphtali** (M4-range, 32GB), **levi** (M4-range, 32GB). These are identified in fleet.toml as the nodes with the most unified memory in the M4 generation.\n\n## Capacity gap vs. RunPod baseline\n\nThe vendor RunPod endpoint is not disclosed at the model level, but the three registered models (`sentinel2_change_siamese`, `sentinel2_landuse_unet`, `sentinel1_flood_unet`) are fine-tuned multi-gigabyte models that would typically target a 48GB A6000 Ada class GPU for batch inference. Religious-corp's EVO-X2 provides 32GB VRAM on a single iGPU with narrower ROCm coverage; the Mac mini fleet provides up to 32GB MLX-unified. **Lower throughput and narrower model coverage are acceptable** for religious-corp use cases (non-paid SaaS, monthly stewardship runs, non-real-time evidence collection) as long as the wire shape remains interoperable with vendor.\n\n---\n\n# Decision\n\n## §1 Analysis tier matrix\n\nFive tiers are defined by workload type, hardware placement, model class, and throughput target. Tiers are evaluated sequentially: preprocessing (T0) always runs first on the receiving Mac mini; downstream tiers are dispatched according to the placement rules in §2.\n\n| Tier | Workload | Backend | Model / toolchain | Throughput target |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **T0 — preprocessing** | Sentinel-1 SAR despeckling (Lee filter / boxcar), Sentinel-2 cloud masking (SCL band), atmospheric correction, COG tile cropping to H3 resolution 7 cells | Mac mini CPU (rasterio + numpy; no GPU) | None — pure CPU pipeline | ~5 s per H3 tile |\n| **T1 — vision-language detection** | vessel-detect in SAR imagery, land-use change flag, anomaly classification from RGB/NIR composite | EVO-X2 ROCm via LiteLLM gateway at `192.168.1.70:4000` (primary); per-node Ollama gemma3:4b (fallback, degraded) | **Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct-4bit** (~5GB, fits in 8GB VRAM slice; ROCm gfx1151 verified via mlx-compatible gguf in Ollama) | 10–30 s per tile (EVO-X2 primary), 45–90 s (fallback) |\n| **T2 — semantic segmentation** | land-cover classification (5-class: water / vegetation / urban / bare soil / agriculture), water body extraction | EVO-X2 ROCm or Mac mini MLX (M4 nodes preferred) | **Florence-2-base** (~450MB, runs on MLX; MPS-accelerated on Apple Silicon); or **SegFormer-b2-finetuned-ade-512-512** (~25MB, CPU-viable) | 5–15 s per tile |\n| **T3 — change detection** | Multi-temporal Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 stack diff (2-date pairs), land-cover delta, SAR backscatter change | Mac mini MLX (M4 nodes: dan, naphtali, levi preferred) | Differential ops via numpy + `torch.mps` (MPS backend on Apple Silicon, no discrete GPU needed); no large model weight required | 10–20 s per tile pair |\n| **T4 — heavy SAR analysis** | SAR interferometry (InSAR phase coherence), oil-spill segmentation, open-water vessel detection (high confidence) | EVO-X2 ROCm only (only realistic local option for >10GB workloads) | **Research spike** — candidate models: distilled OpenSAR-Ship (~7B quantised) or xView2 damage-assessment model distilled to ~13B Q4; neither has verified gfx1151 ROCm inference path as of 2026-05-21 | 30–90 s per scene (estimated; unverified) |\n\n### Analysis type mapping (vendor → tier assignment)\n\nThe three vendor analysis types (`changeDetection`, `landUse`, `sarFlood`) map to tiers as follows:\n\n| Vendor `analysisType` | Tier(s) invoked | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `changeDetection` | T0 + T3 | Sentinel-2 multi-temporal diff; CPU + MPS; no large model needed |\n| `landUse` | T0 + T2 | Sentinel-2 semantic segmentation via Florence-2-base or SegFormer-b2 |\n| `sarFlood` | T0 + T2 (flood mask) | Sentinel-1 SAR despeckling (T0) + binary flood segmentation via SegFormer-b2 (T2); **T4 is not required for basic flood mask** |\n\nHeavy SAR analyses (interferometry, oil spill) are not currently exposed via the vendor lexicon. They are deferred to a future amendment of this ADR (see M4 in §4).\n\n## §2 Placement rules\n\n### P1 — Data locality for T0\n\nT0 (preprocessing) runs on the Mac mini node that originally received the XRPC call. Tile cropping and despeckling produce small output arrays (single H3 tile ≈ 3–15 MB) that are passed to downstream tiers as in-memory bytes or written to local ephemeral storage. No additional network hop is introduced for T0.\n\n### P2 — EVO-X2 dispatch for T1 and T4\n\nT1 (vision-language detection) dispatches to EVO-X2 via the **LiteLLM gateway at `http://192.168.1.70:4000`** (OpenAI-compatible, bearer key `EVO_X2_LITELLM_KEY`). The LiteLLM proxy routes to Ollama at `192.168.1.70:11434` where Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct-4bit is served.\n\nT4 (heavy SAR analysis) dispatches to EVO-X2 via **ComfyUI at `http://192.168.1.70:8188`** using a custom satellite-analysis workflow. This workflow is a research spike (M4 milestone); it does not exist as of this ADR's proposal date. Until M4 is complete, T4 analysis is emitted with `ok: false` and `confidence: 0.0` (degraded — research spike pending flag).\n\n### P3 — Mac mini fleet for T2 and T3\n\nT2 (semantic segmentation) and T3 (change detection) run on Mac mini fleet nodes using per-node MLX or `torch.mps`. Placement preference order:\n\n1. **dan** (M4, 32GB) — preferred for T2 segmentation (Florence-2-base fits easily)\n2. **naphtali** (M4, 32GB) — charter-compliance-leader but also high-memory; used for T2 when dan is busy\n3. **levi** (M4, 32GB) — membership + council orchestration node; available for T2/T3 overflow\n\nT3 (change detection) is lightweight (differential numpy/MPS ops, no model weights) and can run on any Mac mini including lower-memory M1/M2 nodes.\n\n### P4 — EVO-X2 unavailability fallback\n\nIf EVO-X2 is unreachable at analysis time:\n\n- **T1 fallback**: dispatch to per-node Ollama at `http://127.0.0.1:11434` (gemma3:4b — not a vision model; will produce text-only summary with `\"degradedAnalysis\": true` flag in output). Confidence is capped at 0.40 to signal degraded quality.\n- **T4 fallback**: emit `ok: false`, `reason: \"T4_EVO_X2_UNAVAILABLE\"`, `confidence: 0.0`. No local fallback exists for T4 until M4 spike resolves.\n\n### P5 — STAC search (T-1 — not a GPU tier)\n\nThe STAC search task (`maps.sentinel.stac.search` → `task_maps_sentinel_stac_search`) uses no GPU. The vendor implementation's HTTP logic and AOI handling are substrate-neutral and can be ported directly to `maps_sentinel_murakumo.py` without changes to the HTTP logic. The only change is replacing `sync_cursor()` DB writes (Kotoba/Datomic) with AT MST record writes via the etzhayyim substrate (AT Protocol MST + IPFS + Base L2 per ADR-2605172000). STAC search runs on the receiving Mac mini node (CPU-only, no tier assignment).\n\n## §3 Lexicon wire-shape stability\n\n### NSID and field stability\n\nThe existing lexicons `com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.sentinelAnalyze` and `com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.sentinelIngest` (in `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/maps/`) define the wire contract. The religious-corp variant **keeps all required fields byte-identical** to the vendor:\n\n- `sentinelAnalyze` input required fields: `sceneUri` (string), `analysisType` (`changeDetection | landUse | sarFlood`)\n- `sentinelAnalyze` output required fields: `analysisUri` (string), `summary` (string), `confidence` (number 0..1)\n- `sentinelIngest` output required fields: `runId` (string), `scenesIngested` (integer)\n\nNo new required fields are added to the lexicon input/output schemas. Vendor and religious-corp implementations are call-compatible: a BPMN workflow using `com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.sentinelAnalyze` via XRPC will receive a valid response from either implementation.\n\n### Description field adaptation\n\nThe `sentinelAnalyze` lexicon `description` field currently reads:\n\n> \"Run Sentinel scene analysis (change detection / land use / SAR flood) via RunPod Serverless GPU endpoint...\"\n\nPer **ADR-2605214000 §2** PORT-adapted verdict pattern (same as applied to `maps3d/processTile.json`), the `description` field in the religious-corp copy should be updated to replace \"RunPod Serverless GPU endpoint\" with \"Murakumo fleet tiered inference (MLX on Mac mini + ROCm on EVO-X2) per ADR-2605215100\". The NSID, schema, and required fields are unchanged.\n\nThis adaptation is tracked as part of the M0 milestone. The lexicon JSON edit is a single-line description update with no schema impact.\n\n### Collection constants\n\nThe vendor constants `COLLECTION_SCENE = \"com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.satelliteScene\"` and `COLLECTION_ANALYSIS = \"com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.satelliteAnalysis\"` are preserved in the murakumo variant. The `DEFAULT_REPO = \"did:web:maps.etzhayyim.com\"` may be overridden to `did:web:etzhayyim.com` in the religious-corp variant once Step 8 cutover completes, but this is optional and deferred.\n\n## §4 Successor implementation roadmap\n\nThe new implementation file is:\n\n```\n40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/maps_sentinel_murakumo.py\n```\n\nIt does **not** modify or replace the vendor file `maps_sentinel.py`. The vendor file remains operative for `etzhayyim.com` paid SaaS callers. The murakumo variant is a parallel new file that registers different task type names on the LangServer worker:\n\n- `maps.sentinel.stac.search` — identical to vendor (CPU-only STAC logic, ported directly)\n- `maps.sentinel.murakumo.analyze` — replaces `maps.sentinel.runpod.analyze`; uses tiered placement\n\nThe `maps.sentinel.murakumo.analyze` task type is registered alongside `maps.sentinel.runpod.analyze` (which remains disabled for religious-corp callers via `# ETZHAYYIM: vendor-only` import guard per ADR-2605215000 §2.2).\n\n| Milestone | Task | Target date |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | This ADR proposed → active; `sentinelAnalyze.json` description updated (PORT-adapted) | 2026-06-15 |\n| **M1** | T0 preprocessing pipeline: Mac mini rasterio + numpy despeckling (SAR Lee filter), SCL cloud masking, atmospheric correction stub, H3 tile cropping. New file `maps_sentinel_murakumo.py` with `task_maps_sentinel_stac_search` (ported) + `task_maps_sentinel_murakumo_analyze` (T0 only, T1–T4 stubs returning `ok: false`). Unit tests via `tests/test_maps_sentinel_murakumo.py`. | M0 + 30d |\n| **M2** | T1: Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct-4bit dispatch to EVO-X2 via LiteLLM gateway; verify ROCm gfx1151 inference path with a test SAR tile; implement T1 fallback (gemma3:4b local degraded path); wire `changeDetection` and `landUse` to T0 + T1 for initial output | M1 + 30d |\n| **M3** | T2 + T3: Florence-2-base via `mlx_lm` on M4 nodes for land-cover segmentation; SegFormer-b2 ONNX fallback for SAR flood mask; numpy + `torch.mps` differential ops for change detection; `sarFlood` analysis type fully operational end-to-end | M2 + 45d |\n| **M4** | T4 heavy SAR (research spike): InSAR coherence via custom ComfyUI workflow on EVO-X2; OpenSAR-Ship distilled Q4 candidate evaluation on gfx1151; oil-spill segmentation. Slip allowed — block on gfx1151 ROCm coverage for large models. Report back as ADR amendment. | M3 + 60d (slip allowed) |\n| **M5** | Retire `maps.sentinel.runpod.analyze` for religious-corp callers: `LandStewardshipMonitoringCell` and `AuditWitnessCell` wired to `maps.sentinel.murakumo.analyze`; import guard added to `maps_sentinel.py` per ADR-2605215000 §2.2; `PYKOTODAMA-MIGRATION-NOTES.md` maps_sentinel row marked complete | Tied to Step 8 legal registration cutover |\n\n## §5 Status amendments\n\nThis ADR **extends** (does not supersede) ADR-2605215000:\n\n- **ADR-2605215000 §3 REIMPLEMENT item** for `maps_sentinel.py` is now made concrete by this ADR. The companion `PYKOTODAMA-MIGRATION-NOTES.md` maps_sentinel row should be updated to reference ADR-2605215100 as the design authority for the murakumo variant.\n- This ADR does not change the RunPod prohibition (established by ADR-2605215000 §1), the substrate boundary (ADR-2605172000), or the EVO-X2 placement contract (ADR-2605202345). It sharpens the implementation plan for one specific REIMPLEMENT target.\n\n---\n\n# Consequences\n\n1. **REIMPLEMENT closure for the heaviest kotodama target**: `maps_sentinel.py` was the most structurally complex RunPod coupling in the kotodama codebase — it has custom polling logic, a model registry, and a LangChain stage pipeline. This ADR closes the design gap; M1–M3 execution closes the engineering gap. The Step 8 cutover sub-list now has a concrete implementation path.\n\n2. **Vendor wire shape preserved for interop**: The `com.etzhayyim.apps.maps.sentinelAnalyze` lexicon required fields are byte-identical between vendor and religious-corp variants. A BPMN process using `sceneUri` + `analysisType` inputs and `analysisUri` + `confidence` outputs works against both backends. Description text is the only lexicon field changed (PORT-adapted pattern from ADR-2605214000 §2).\n\n3. **Capacity gap honestly documented**: The religious-corp fleet has no NVIDIA 48GB equivalent. ROCm gfx1151 with 32GB UMA is the best available GPU; MLX on M4 Mac mini provides 32GB unified with better model coverage for Apple-Silicon-optimised weights. SAR interferometry (T4) remains a research spike — no gfx1151-verified InSAR pipeline exists as of 2026-05-21. This is not a blocker for M1–M3 (T0–T3 cover all three vendor analysis types).\n\n4. **Operations simpler than RunPod**: No RunPod billing, no cold-start latency (RunPod Serverless can take 30–120s to cold-start), no `/runsync` vs `/run` + poll protocol divergence, no `RUNPOD_KEY` or `RUNPOD_ENDPOINT_ID_MAPS` secrets to rotate. EVO-X2 is LAN-only warm infrastructure. Mac mini fleet nodes are always warm.\n\n5. **EVO-X2 SPoF risk mitigated by degraded path**: T1 falls back to per-node gemma3:4b (text-only, confidence capped at 0.40) when EVO-X2 is unavailable. T0, T2, T3 continue fully operational during EVO-X2 downtime since they run on Mac mini fleet. Only T4 (research spike, not yet implemented) is hard-blocked on EVO-X2 availability. Medium-term mitigation: a second M4 Ultra Mac mini (128GB unified) would absorb T1 and T2 as well; tracked as `replica_recommended` in fleet.toml `[inference_backends.evo-x2.failover]`.\n\n6. **Per-node gemma3:4b fallback is genuinely degraded for vision tasks**: gemma3:4b is a text-only model (no vision tokens). The T1 fallback path produces a text summary based on scene metadata only (platform, datetime, cloudCover, bbox) with no pixel-level analysis. This is explicitly marked as `\"degradedAnalysis\": true` in the output and confidence capped at 0.40. Religious-corp callers (LandStewardshipMonitoringCell, AuditWitnessCell) must handle this flag.\n\n---\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n## A1. Keep RunPod for SAR analysis only; use Murakumo for optical Sentinel-2\n\nProposal: Allow RunPod specifically for `sarFlood` (Sentinel-1 SAR) since SAR analysis is computationally heavier, while routing `changeDetection` and `landUse` to Murakumo.\n\n**Reject**: This is precisely the slippery-slope pattern that ADR-2605215000 §1.2 conditions and ADR-2605191346 §2 reject for K8s. A \"SAR-only carve-out\" for commercial GPU rental creates a partial dependency that grows: the next heavy workload would justify another carve-out. The substrate sovereignty invariant requires full inference independence. The T4 research spike is the honest alternative — if SAR interferometry cannot be solved locally within the hardware budget, it is documented as a research spike rather than handed back to commercial cloud.\n\n## A2. Vultr VKE GPU node dedicated to Sentinel analysis\n\nProposal: Provision a Vultr VKE node with an NVIDIA GPU (Vultr A100 or L40S node pool) specifically for satellite analysis, separate from the general Murakumo fleet.\n\n**Reject**: ADR-2605191346 explicitly prohibits commercial K8s (Vultr VKE) for etzhayyim workloads. This proposal violates two invariants simultaneously: the no-commercial-K8s rule and the no-commercial-GPU-rental rule (ADR-2605215000). The satellite analysis workload does not justify a structural exception to either.\n\n## A3. AWS SageMaker or GCP Vertex AI batch inference for SAR\n\nProposal: Use batch cloud ML inference (SageMaker batch transform or Vertex AI prediction) billed as a one-time run rather than an ongoing subscription, avoiding the \"rental\" framing.\n\n**Reject**: The substrate-fit conditions (ADR-2605215000 §2.1) prohibit any commercial cloud inference, including batch invocations. \"Pay-per-call\" cloud inference is structurally identical to \"pay-per-run\" RunPod — operational availability is contingent on a commercial vendor's service. Billing model (subscription vs. pay-per-call) does not change the structural dependency. Additionally, Sentinel scene data would need to be uploaded to AWS/GCP, which introduces data sovereignty concerns for religiously significant land monitoring.\n\n## A4. Drop SAR analysis entirely from religious-corp scope\n\nProposal: Serve only Sentinel-2 optical analyses (changeDetection, landUse) and mark `sarFlood` and all SAR workloads as VENDOR-ONLY.\n\n**Reject**: `sarFlood` is directly needed for the land trust monitoring use case (ADR-2605192245) where donated parcels include coastal and riverside plots (ADR-2605192330 extended sovereignty). Sentinel-1 SAR penetrates cloud cover and provides flood-mapping capability even during typhoon seasons when Sentinel-2 optical data is unavailable. The kuni-umi survey (ADR-2605201400) similarly relies on SAR for construction-phase monitoring of infrastructure projects. Dropping SAR entirely would leave these religious-corp governance processes without automated satellite evidence during the very weather conditions where evidence is most needed.\n\n---\n\n# References\n\n- **depends_on**:\n  - ADR-2605191346 — etzhayyim is Vultr-free / no commercial K8s (parallel substrate sovereignty invariant)\n  - ADR-2605202345 — EVO-X2 GMKtec integration (hardware spec, endpoints, ROCm verification, failover contract)\n  - ADR-2605215000 — etzhayyim inference Murakumo-fleet-only / RunPod constitutionally prohibited (parent ADR; §2.3 marks maps_sentinel.py REIMPLEMENT)\n- **related**:\n  - ADR-2605201400 — kuni-umi planetary infra fleet (SiteSurveyCell, AuditWitnessCell use SAR analysis)\n  - ADR-2605192245 — etzhayyim global land sovereignty (land trust monitoring use case for Sentinel analysis)\n  - ADR-2605172000 — kotoba substrate (AT MST + IPFS + Base L2 replaces Kotoba/Datomic for scene/analysis record writes)\n- **Implementation target**: `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/maps_sentinel_murakumo.py` (new file; do not modify vendor `maps_sentinel.py`)\n- **Step 8 cutover sub-list**: `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/PYKOTODAMA-MIGRATION-NOTES.md` (sister document; maps_sentinel row)\n- **Lexicons**: `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/maps/sentinelAnalyze.json`, `sentinelIngest.json` (wire contract; description-only PORT-adapted per ADR-2605214000 §2)\n- **Adjacent lexicons**: `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/maps3d/README.edn` (PORT verdict patterns used as reference for lexicon adaptation)\n- **Fleet config**: `50-infra/murakumo/fleet.toml` — node capabilities, EVO-X2 inference_backends endpoints, per-node Ollama fallback\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605215100-etzhayyim-maps-sentinel-mlx-murakumo-fleet.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "etzhayyim-maps-sentinel-mlx-murakumo-fleet", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-21", :adr/date "2026-05-21", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605201400-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-planetary-infra-fleet" "adr-2605192245-etzhayyim-global-land-sovereignty"], :adr/authoritative_for ["Sentinel-1 SAR + Sentinel-2 multispectral analysis on etzhayyim fleet" "Tiered GPU/MLX placement for satellite imagery workloads" "maps_sentinel_murakumo.py REIMPLEMENT successor implementation roadmap"]}]
